From 05d02d243414ea5f5d83a863fb82b061a1bec31e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:25:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] RetroPlayer: Free the textures of renderers that are no
 longer drawn

The render manager kept every renderer it made until the stream was
reconfigured or stopped. Each filter previewed in the video filter
dialog left its renderer behind, with its shaders and textures, so
browsing filters grew GPU memory until Kodi was killed for running out
of memory on an Android Shield.

A renderer that nothing asked for in the last frame now frees its frame,
the textures its passes draw into and the preset's look-up textures, by
the same one-frame rule that IsVisible() uses. It keeps its compiled
shaders, so a filter that comes back into view only loads its look-up
textures again rather than being compiled again.
